# Fable of the Mirror-Breaker through all three chapters (CR 714): chapter I (as it enters) makes a Goblin Shaman, chapter II
# (the lore counter added after Bot1's draw step on turn 3) discards a Mountain and draws a card, and chapter III on
# turn 5 exiles the Saga and returns it transformed (CR 712.14a) as Reflection of Kiki-Jiki, a 2/2 Enchantment Creature
# that is no longer a Saga and has no lore counter (so nothing sacrifices it). On turn 7 it copies the Goblin Shaman, a
# nonlegendary creature (CR 707.9b: the token has haste), and the copy is sacrificed at the beginning of that turn's end step.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Fable of the Mirror-Breaker
Mountain x3
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

